# Lucairn kit — `witness-central` topology, environment set
#
# Copy to `contrib/witness-central/witness-central.env` and fill in. Pass it as
# a SECOND --env-file after customer.env; nothing here overlaps customer.env, so
# the stock install is unaffected when this overlay is not applied.
#
# Full procedure, including the CA ceremony that produces the files referenced
# below: docs/WITNESS_CENTRAL_RUNBOOK.md

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# host:port of the CENTRAL witness's claim-intake port. This is the address the
# gateway, sanitizer, id-bridge and audit emitters dial.
#
# Reachability check before you start the stack:
#   nc -vz <host> 50057
#
# Note this is a gRPC port, not HTTP — a browser or plain `curl` will not give a
# meaningful answer, and "connection refused" here is a firewall/NAT problem,
# not a Lucairn one.
LUCAIRN_CENTRAL_WITNESS_ADDR=witness.example.eu:50057

# Host directory holding THIS DEVICE's client credential. Must contain exactly:
#
#   ca.pem      the shared CA bundle that issued the central witness's server
#               leaf (NOT a public root store — see the runbook on why)
#   client.pem  this device's client leaf, issued by that CA
#   client.key  its private key, mode 0600, never shared between devices
#
# Mounted read-only at /etc/lucairn/witness-client in every emitter container and
# wired via the WITNESS-SCOPED LCR_WITNESS_MTLS_* variables — deliberately not
# the mesh-wide DSA_MTLS_* ones, which are process-wide and would also force
# every local dial (gateway→audit, →id-bridge, →inference, sanitizer→reid-guard)
# onto mTLS against peers that are still plaintext.
LUCAIRN_WITNESS_CLIENT_CERT_DIR=/opt/lucairn/certs/witness-client

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The mTLS latch. Leave at "true".
#
# Setting it to anything else disengages the fail-closed behaviour: an
# incomplete or missing credential then falls back to a CLEARTEXT dial to
# LUCAIRN_CENTRAL_WITNESS_ADDR, which puts the sanitizer's
# redaction_manifest_body — the raw placeholder→original map — on the public
# internet with no warning in any log. The value is matched strictly against
# "true"; "1" and "yes" read as DISENGAGED.
#
# There is no legitimate reason to turn this off in a witness-central
# deployment. It exists as a knob only so the same images can still run the
# stock LAN topology.
LCR_WITNESS_REQUIRE_MTLS=true

# ── Required (cont.) ────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Certificate RETRIEVAL address (:50058), a different port with a different
# credential family (WITNESS_MTLS_*).
#
# REQUIRED, not optional. An earlier revision of this overlay let it default to
# the local `veil-witness:50058`. The laptop no longer runs a witness, so there
# is nothing local to fall back to: leaving this unset now fails the compose
# render with a sentence naming this variable, which is a better outcome than
# the gateway's /verify and /summary surfaces failing at request time with a
# connection error.
#
# The gateway's WITNESS_MTLS_* CLIENT triple is wired automatically by the
# overlay from LUCAIRN_WITNESS_CLIENT_CERT_DIR — the same three files serve both
# hops. You do NOT need to set WITNESS_MTLS_* by hand.
#
# ⚠️ Without a client triple the cert server has NO client authentication and NO
# authorization, and GetCertificate/ExportCertificates return certificates
# carrying redaction_manifest_body. The runbook's ingress guidance is to publish
# :50057 broadly and :50058 per-device.
LUCAIRN_CENTRAL_WITNESS_CERT_ADDR=witness.example.eu:50058

# ── Optional (cont.) ────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Override the TLS ServerName the gateway verifies on the :50058 hop. Set this
# when the address you publish differs from the SAN the CA ceremony issued on
# the central witness's server leaf — otherwise the handshake fails with a
# hostname mismatch that reads like a certificate problem.
# LUCAIRN_CENTRAL_WITNESS_SERVER_NAME=witness

# ── MANDATORY MANUAL STEP: retire the local witness signing key ─────
#
# `bin/lucairn init` generates LCR_WITNESS_SIGNING_KEY (and its VEIL_ alias)
# into customer.env for every topology. This overlay cannot reach into that
# generator, so the key is still sitting in your customer.env after you adopt
# witness-central — unused, but present.
#
# The PRD's success criterion is that the laptop holds NO signing key in the
# witness role. "Unused" is not "absent": a key on the machine is a key that can
# be used, and the whole point of a central witness is that the operator cannot
# sign evidence about their own conduct.
#
# After your first successful witness-central turn, delete these lines from
# customer.env and recreate the stack:
#
#   LCR_WITNESS_SIGNING_KEY=...
#   VEIL_WITNESS_SIGNING_KEY=...
#
# Keep LCR_WITNESS_PUBLIC_KEY — the gateway publishes it at
# /.well-known/veil-keys.json and verifiers need it. Replace its VALUE with the
# CENTRAL witness's public key, or the discovery surface will advertise a key
# that signed nothing.
#
# See docs/WITNESS_CENTRAL_RUNBOOK.md § "Retire the local signing key".
